codex
The patch builds and preserves the core mapping path, but the new stmap77 reconstruction diagnostics are scoped over both stmap65 mapping passes, making the reported diagnostic data inaccurate for the final network.

Review comment:

- [P2] Limit reconstruction tracing to the final stmap65 map — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/base/abci/abcStmap_77.c:85-86
  With the default stmap65 flow, `Abc_CommandStmap65` first calls `Abc_NtkMap` to build the temporary feedback network and then calls it again for the final remap. Because this enables reconstruction tracing before invoking the whole command, the `reconstruct-*` rows and summary combine the throwaway first reconstruction with the final one, which double-counts emits/cache hits and can report phases or gates that are not in the final mapped network. Enable/reset the trace only around the final remap, or tag the pass so the analysis can filter it.
The patch builds and preserves the core mapping path, but the new stmap77 reconstruction diagnostics are scoped over both stmap65 mapping passes, making the reported diagnostic data inaccurate for the final network.

Review comment:

- [P2] Limit reconstruction tracing to the final stmap65 map — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/base/abci/abcStmap_77.c:85-86
  With the default stmap65 flow, `Abc_CommandStmap65` first calls `Abc_NtkMap` to build the temporary feedback network and then calls it again for the final remap. Because this enables reconstruction tracing before invoking the whole command, the `reconstruct-*` rows and summary combine the throwaway first reconstruction with the final one, which double-counts emits/cache hits and can report phases or gates that are not in the final mapped network. Enable/reset the trace only around the final remap, or tag the pass so the analysis can filter it.
